.TH UNIM-GUI-QT 1 "April 2026" "UNIM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-gui\-qt \- UNIM Hanja and special-character popups (Qt6/QML)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-gui\-qt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unim\-gui\-qt
is the Qt6/QML alternative GUI for the UNIM input method engine. It
provides Hanja conversion and special-character / emoji search popups
without the GTK4/libadwaita dependency, primarily for KDE Plasma and
other Qt-centric desktops where pulling in libadwaita is undesirable.
.PP
Unlike
.BR unim\-gui\-gtk (1)
this front-end does not host a settings dialog; configuration must be
performed via
.BR unim\-config (1)
or by launching
.B unim\-gui\-gtk \-\-settings
when GTK is available.
.PP
The program communicates with
.B unim\-daemon
over the
.B org.atit.unim.InputMethod
D-Bus session interface and is normally activated on demand by the
daemon when a Hanja popup is requested.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
Configuration file shared with
.BR unim\-config (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-config (1),
.BR unim\-gui\-gtk (1)
